  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 135 AM EST Wed Nov 11 2026\n\n- Rain showers today, then cooler with Lake Effect rain/snow\n\nRain showers advancing eastward from Minnesota into Wisconsin this\nmorning are associated with a clipper low/digging northern stream\nshortwave trough. Expect the rain to move into northwest forecast\narea this morning then spread to the southeast in the afternoon. \n\nThe trough merges with a retrograding upper low over eastern\nCanada., leading to an amplified pattern across the CONUS through\nthe weekend, with strong northerly flow bringing lake effect rain\nand snow showers and cool temperatures for Thursday through \nSaturday. The immediate lakeshore should remain rain due to\nmodification by the relatively warm lake surface temperatures.\nInland will see some snow and perhaps light accumulations on\nunpaved surfaces. Travel impacts are not expected since the\nheavier lake effect bands are expected to remain offshore.",
